        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Select Theorem4.17 with d=3 and the R_z action specified in Section4.6: G=R2 semidirect_phi R has a cocompact lattice Lambda, z0 is the lattice-rational chosen nontrivial torsion-direction vector in image(phi_x0-id), and R_z0 intersect Lambda is a lattice. The Mostow circle, period matrix Sigma and lattice monodromy conventions4.2–4.4 are retained. The full author coset, lattice-action, fiber crossed-product and equivariant Morita-module computations4.16–4.17 are present;4.18/4.19 supply the monodromy interpretation. Existing Green imprimitivity, semidirect crossed-product decomposition and noncommutative-torus Morita facts are genuinely prior background. The conclusion is Morita equivalence, not isomorphism of the original crossed product to a commutative space, and the exceptional fibers are treated as in the source. Higher-dimensional and separate classical H-flux branches are contextual only."
      },
